ry guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"MOB01","name":"90/90 Hip Rotation","video_id":"pW9QAqCau3Y","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/pW9QAqCau3Y","before":{"description":"Sit with both knees bent at about a right angle. Use your hands for support if needed. Turn slowly from your hips in the direction your coach shows you.","purpose":"Explore comfortable hip rotation with control.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Move slowly from your hips. Avoid: Forcing either knee to the floor.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Sit in the 90/90 position shown, supporting yourself with your hands if needed. Move between the demonstrated hip positions slowly within your available range. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Explore comfortable hip rotation with control.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Sit tall. Move from hips. Use a small range. Avoid: Forcing either knee to the floor, twisting through pain or using momentum.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"MOB02","name":"Kneeling Couch Stretch","video_id":"hSX1K5LVGJw","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/hSX1K5LVGJw","before":{"description":"Kneel with padding under the back knee and set the back foot on the support as assigned. Ease into a gentle stretch at the front of your hip.","purpose":"Gently explore front-of-hip and thigh flexibility.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stay tall and breathe. Avoid: Arching your back to feel a stronger stretch.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Use a padded kneeling position with the rear foot supported as demonstrated. Keep the ribs settled and move into a gentle stretch without forcing the back knee or lower back. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Gently explore front-of-hip and thigh flexibility.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Squeeze rear glute gently. Ribs settled. Breathe. Avoid: Arching the back, pressing painfully into the kneecap or forcing the heel toward the hip.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"MOB03","name":"Calf Stretch","video_id":"iHlzoeOT9ZA","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/iHlzoeOT9ZA","before":{"description":"Hold a firm support and set your feet and knees as your coach shows you. Keep the stretching heel down as you ease forward.","purpose":"Gently explore calf and ankle range.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Keep your heel down. Avoid: Bouncing into the stretch.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Use a stable support and the foot and knee position shown. Keep the stretching heel down and shift into a gentle calf stretch, breathing steadily. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Gently explore calf and ankle range.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Heel grounded. Foot forward. Ease into it. Avoid: Bouncing, turning the foot outward to gain range or pushing through sharp pain.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"MOB04","name":"Diaphragmatic Breathing","video_id":"gSrUPWTSU-g","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/gSrUPWTSU-g","before":{"description":"Sit or lie down and relax your shoulders. Breathe gently into your lower ribs, then breathe out slowly. If you feel light-headed, return to normal breathing.","purpose":"Practise relaxed breathing and a controlled reset.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Soft shoulders, easy exhale. Avoid: Forcing a deep breath or holding it.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Lie or sit comfortably with the neck and shoulders relaxed. Breathe gently into the lower ribs and abdomen, then let the air out slowly without straining. Use the breathing time assigned; return to normal breathing if you feel light-headed.","purpose":"Practise relaxed breathing and a controlled reset.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Soft shoulders. Quiet breath. Long easy exhale. Avoid: Forcing deep breaths, holding the breath or continuing if you feel dizzy.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"MOB05","name":"Shoulder Airplane","video_id":"7vF74hmyxPc","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/7vF74hmyxPc","before":{"description":"Ask your coach to show the starting position and arm path. Move your arms slowly as shown and stay in a comfortable range.","purpose":"Explore shoulder movement while controlling the trunk.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Keep your neck relaxed. Avoid: Shrugging your shoulders to lift your arms farther.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Use the starting position and arm path demonstrated by Coach Du. Move the arms smoothly through a comfortable range while keeping the ribs and neck relaxed; confirm the variant with Coach Du if unclear. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Explore shoulder movement while controlling the trunk.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Easy shoulders. Quiet ribs. Smooth motion. Avoid: Shrugging, forcing the arms behind the body or arching the back to gain range.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"MOB06","name":"Couch Stretch","video_id":"wEe7pfcm8ns","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/wEe7pfcm8ns","before":{"description":"Set up in the supported position your coach shows you. Pad your knee if you kneel. Ease into a gentle stretch and breathe normally.","purpose":"Gently explore front-of-hip and thigh flexibility.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stay tall and breathe. Avoid: Arching your lower back to go deeper.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied. Potential alternate demonstration of MOB02 Kneeling Couch Stretch; existing record/video preserved pending comparison.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Use the supported position shown in this couch-stretch demonstration and pad any kneeling contact. Ease into a gentle stretch with ribs settled; match the demonstrated variant rather than forcing depth. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Gently explore front-of-hip and thigh flexibility.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Gentle glute squeeze. Ribs settled. Breathe. Avoid: Forcing the back knee, arching the lower back or pulling the foot farther than comfortable.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied. Potential alternate demonstration of MOB02 Kneeling Couch Stretch; existing record/video preserved pending comparison.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"MOB07","name":"Seated Pigeon — Knee-to-Chest Rock","video_id":"Uj7FxJRnja8","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/Uj7FxJRnja8","before":{"description":"Sit in the position your coach shows you. Support the leg and gently rock the knee a little toward your chest, then release.","purpose":"Explore comfortable seated hip mobility with a knee-to-chest action.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Small, slow rocks. Avoid: Pulling hard on the knee.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Sit in the pigeon position demonstrated. Support the leg as shown and use a small knee-to-chest rocking action from the hip, staying upright and within a comfortable range. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Explore comfortable seated hip mobility with a knee-to-chest action.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Sit tall. Gentle rock. Move from the hip. Avoid: Pulling hard on the knee, rounding to force range or continuing through joint pain.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"MOB08","name":"Seated Pigeon — Knee Push Away","video_id":"ZkRmZh3gxLU","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/ZkRmZh3gxLU","before":{"description":"Sit in the position your coach shows you and support the leg. Gently guide the knee away, then release the pressure slowly.","purpose":"Explore comfortable hip opening in a seated pigeon position.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Move only as far as feels comfortable. Avoid: Pressing hard on the knee.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Sit in the demonstrated pigeon position and support the leg. Gently guide the knee away only within a comfortable hip range, then release the pressure with control. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Explore comfortable hip opening in a seated pigeon position.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Sit tall. Light pressure. Easy breathing. Avoid: Forcing the knee down, bouncing or mistaking knee pain for a useful stretch.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"MOB09","name":"Seated Pigeon — Figure-4 Forward Lean","video_id":"aYdisAtwlNA","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/aYdisAtwlNA","before":{"description":"Sit with one ankle across the opposite thigh as shown. Keep your back long and lean forward a little from the hips, then ease back.","purpose":"Explore hip flexibility through a controlled forward lean.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Lean from your hips. Avoid: Rounding your back to go farther.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Set the seated figure-4 position demonstrated. Keep the spine long and hinge forward gently from the hips until a comfortable stretch is felt, then ease back. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Explore hip flexibility through a controlled forward lean.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Long spine. Hinge from hips. Gentle stretch. Avoid: Rounding deeply, pushing the knee down or forcing a painful range.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"MOB10","name":"Body Circles Mobility Series","video_id":"BeWvd3n4lk0","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/BeWvd3n4lk0","before":{"description":"Ask Coach Du to confirm the movement sequence before you start. Use the order and positions your coach gives you.","purpose":"Explore comfortable joint movement through the demonstrated body-circle series.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Make small, slow circles. Avoid: Guessing the order or rushing between positions.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied. Preserve as one series; demonstrated movement order has not been verified.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: sequence-pending-coach-verification; general-cues-only; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Sequence not yet verified. Watch the full demonstration first. Ask Coach Du to confirm the movement sequence and starting positions before your first session; use only the assigned variations in the confirmed order. Keep transitions controlled and use the sets, repetitions or time on your training sheet.","purpose":"Explore comfortable joint movement through the demonstrated body-circle series.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Small circles. Easy rhythm