me on your training sheet.","purpose":"Explore controlled mobility through the demonstrated floor-based series.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Move smoothly. Support your weight. Easy breathing. Avoid: Forcing end positions, rushing floor transitions or continuing through joint pain.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied. Preserve as one series; demonstrated movement order has not been verified.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: sequence-pending-coach-verification; general-cues-only; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY01","name":"Snap Down","video_id":"Dv6blgFNo28","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/Dv6blgFNo28","before":{"description":"Stand tall on a clear surface that gives you grip. Drop quickly into a shallow landing with your hips and knees bent. Hold still.","purpose":"Practise moving quickly into a controlled landing position.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Quiet feet, then freeze. Avoid: Landing with stiff knees. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Stand tall on a clear, non-slip surface. Drop quickly into the athletic position shown, then become still with hips, knees and ankles softly bent. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise moving quickly into a controlled landing position.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Quick down. Quiet feet. Own the position. Avoid: Slamming the feet, landing with straight knees or letting knees collapse inward.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY02","name":"Broad Jump + Stick","video_id":"SZhqfsybVp8","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/SZhqfsybVp8","before":{"description":"Check that the landing area is clear. Jump forward from both feet, bend your knees as you land and hold still before the next jump.","purpose":"Develop horizontal jumping power and controlled two-foot landings.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Land quietly and hold. Avoid: Jumping farther than you can land in balance. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Stand with both feet stable and a clear landing area. Jump forward as assigned, absorb through hips, knees and ankles, then hold balance before resetting. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Develop horizontal jumping power and controlled two-foot landings.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push forward. Land quietly. Hold still. Avoid: Chasing distance beyond control, landing stiff-legged or falling forward after contact.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY03","name":"Two-Leg Pogos","video_id":"l6kbuPq2aHU","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/l6kbuPq2aHU","before":{"description":"Stand tall on a surface with good grip. Make small, steady bounces on both feet with soft knees.","purpose":"Practise small, rhythmic two-foot ankle contacts.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Low bounces, steady beat. Avoid: Bending into a deep squat between bounces. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Stand tall on a suitable, non-slip training surface. Make low, continuous jumps from both feet, keeping the knees softly responsive and contacts under the body. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise small, rhythmic two-foot ankle contacts.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stay tall. Small bounce. Even rhythm. Avoid: Deep squatting, rigidly straight knees or continuing when contacts become heavy or uneven.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY04","name":"Drop to Hold","video_id":"ZXRiDxgcJZE","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/ZXRiDxgcJZE","before":{"description":"Start at the height or position your coach assigns. If using a box, step off it. Bend your hips and knees as you land and hold still.","purpose":"Practise absorbing a drop and holding a stable landing.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Land softly and hold. Avoid: Jumping up off the box or bouncing straight back up. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Use only the starting height or position Coach Du assigns. Drop into the demonstrated landing, absorb through hips, knees and ankles and become still before resetting; if using a box, step off rather than jump up first. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise absorbing a drop and holding a stable landing.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Absorb softly. Knees follow toes. Hold balance. Avoid: Adding height, rebounding immediately or landing with rigid legs.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY05","name":"Single-Leg Hop + Stick","video_id":"IEGb_26TH6Q","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/IEGb_26TH6Q","before":{"description":"Balance on the leg you were assigned. Hop as prescribed, land on that same leg and get steady before the next hop.","purpose":"Develop control of a single-leg hop and landing.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Land softly and hold still. Avoid: Letting your landing knee drop inward. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Stand balanced on the assigned leg with a clear landing space. Hop as prescribed, absorb on that leg and hold balance before the next repetition. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Develop control of a single-leg hop and landing.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push with control. Soft knee. Stick the landing. Avoid: Chasing distance, letting the knee collapse inward or hopping again before balance is regained.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY06","name":"Forward / Backward Pogos","video_id":"_cOsAkPbA-Q","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/_cOsAkPbA-Q","before":{"description":"Start tall on both feet with space in front and behind. Make small bounces forward and back with a steady rhythm.","purpose":"Practise rhythmic forward and backward ankle contacts.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Keep the bounces small. Avoid: Taking long jumps that pull you off balance. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Start tall with both feet under you on a clear surface. Make small two-foot contacts forward and backward as shown, keeping the distance short and rhythm even. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise rhythmic forward and backward ankle contacts.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Small travel. Quick rhythm. Feet under body. Avoid: Large leaps, drifting out of balance or letting contacts become loud and heavy.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY07","name":"Single-Leg Pogos","video_id":"GE64gjOBNzU","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/GE64gjOBNzU","before":{"description":"Balance on the leg you were assigned. Make low, steady bounces under that hip, using the other leg for balance as shown.","purpose":"Practise rhythmic ankle contacts and balance on one leg.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stay tall and bounce low. Avoid: Continuing once your contacts get heavy or uneven. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Balance on the assigned leg on a suitable training surface. Make low repeated contacts under the hip, using the other leg for balance as shown. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise rhythmic ankle contacts and balance on one leg.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Tall body. Small bounce. Steady rhythm. Avoid: Hopping too high, letting the knee collapse inward or continuing after rhythm is lost.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY08","name":"Jump Squat + Stick","video_id":"v20rnNpFVfE","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/v20rnNpFVfE","before":{"description":"Start with your feet set to jump. Bend your hips and knees, jump straight up and land softly. Hold still before the next rep.","purpose":"Develop vertical jumping power with a controlled stop on landing.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Jump up, land and hold. Avoid: Taking the next jump before you are steady. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Start in a comfortable athletic stance. Dip and jump vertically, then absorb the landing and hold still before resetting for the next repetition. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Develop vertical jumping power with a controlled stop on landing.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push tall. Land softly. Hold balance. Avoid: Landing stiff-legged, knees collapsing inward or rushing into the next jump.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY09","name":"Repeated Vertical Jumps","video_id":"vlToXrdgJos","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/vlToXrdgJos","before":{"description":"Check the landing space is clear. Jump straight up and land softly each time. Use the rhythm your coach gives you.","purpose":"Practise repeated vertical jumping with consistent alignment.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Land quietly on each jump. Avoid: Keeping going when landings get heavy or uneven. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Use a clear landing area and the jump rhythm Coach Du prescribes. Jump vertically, absorb each landing and move into the next jump while posture remains controlled. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise repeated vertical jumping with consistent alignment.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push up. Land aligned. Keep rhythm. Avoid: Chasing height after technique fades, rigid landings or adding extra contacts.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY10","name":"Lateral Bound + Stick","video_id":"B0Yd3lnlW2E","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/B0Yd3lnlW2E","before":{"description":"Balance on one leg with clear space to the side. Push sideways, land on the other leg and hold your balance.","purpose":"Develop lateral power and single-leg landing control.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push sideways, then hold. Avoid: Letting the landing knee fall inward. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Balance on one leg with clear space to the side. Push sideways onto the other leg, absorb through that hip and knee and hold still before resetting. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Develop lateral power and single-leg landing control.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push sideways. Land softly. Hips level. Avoid: Reaching too far, knee collapse or stepping again before balance is controlled.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY11","name":"Continuous Skater Bounds","video_id":"8YtmCCxMFZQ","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/8YtmCCxMFZQ","before":{"description":"Clear space on either side. Jump sideways from one foot to the other. Control each landing before you push back.","purpose":"Practise continuous lateral jumping and controlled weight transfer.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Control the landing, then push back. Avoid: Going wider or faster than you can control. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Set a clear side-to-side space. Bound from one leg to the other as assigned, controlling each landing before directing the next push. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise continuous lateral jumping and controlled weight transfer.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push across. Control contact. Keep rhythm. Avoid: Chasing distance, uncontrolled trunk sway or continuing when landings become unstable.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY12","name":"Continuous Bench-Assisted Single-Leg Pogos","video_id":"FNmXU6Y0dSA","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/FNmXU6Y0dSA","before":{"description":"Make sure the bench cannot move. Set the supported leg in the position your coach shows you. Make low bounces on the other leg.","purpose":"Practise continuous vertical single-leg contacts with bench assistance.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Small bounces under your hip. Avoid: Letting the bench or supported leg shift. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Secure the bench and position the assisted leg exactly as shown. Make small vertical contacts on the working leg, keeping the support steady and rhythm even. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise continuous vertical single-leg contacts with bench assistance.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stay tall. Bounce vertically. Light contacts. Avoid: Using a loose bench, pushing excessively through the assisted leg or letting the knee collapse inward.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY13","name":"Bench-Assisted Forward & Backward Single-Leg Pogos","video_id":"HmGQh619zLE","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/HmGQh619zLE","before":{"description":"Make sure the bench cannot move and set the supported leg as shown. Use the working leg to make short bounces forward and back.","purpose":"Practise forward and backward single-leg contacts with bench assistance.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Keep the bounces short. Avoid: Reaching so far that you lose balance. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Secure the bench and set the assisted leg as demonstrated. Use short forward and backward contacts on the working leg while keeping the support position controlled. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise forward and backward single-leg contacts with bench assistance.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Small travel. Tall posture. Even rhythm. Avoid: Leaping too far, twisting the pelvis or losing safe contact with the bench.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY14","name":"Bench-Assisted Triangle Single-Leg Pogos","video_id":"viTsnTKQSe8","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/viTsnTKQSe8","before":{"description":"Make sure the bench cannot move and set the supported leg as shown. Make small bounces on the working leg along the triangle your coach shows you.","purpose":"Practise controlled single-leg contacts in three directions with bench assistance.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Keep each bounce small. Avoid: Rushing around the triangle when you lose balance. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Secure the bench and match the supported position shown. Follow the demonstrated triangle path with short contacts on the working leg, resetting if balance changes. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise controlled single-leg contacts in three directions with bench assistance.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Small triangle. Knee follows toes. Steady rhythm. Avoid: Widening the triangle beyond control, twisting the knee or using an unstable bench.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY15","name":"Seated Tuck-to-Vertical Jump","video_id":"GIevwzw8new","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/GIevwzw8new","before":{"description":"Use a seat that cannot move and check the landing area. Ask your coach to show the tuck and seated position. Jump up from that position, land softly and reset.","purpose":"Practise producing a vertical jump from the demonstrated seated position.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Jump straight up, land softly. Avoid: Adding a bounce straight after landing. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Secure the seat and clear the landing space. Match the demonstrated tuck and seated position, then drive into the vertical jump as shown; absorb the landing and reset rather than adding extra jumps. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise producing a vertical jump from the demonstrated seated position.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Drive up. Land softly. Reset with control. Avoid: Rocking beyond control, using an unstable seat or adding an unassigned landing or repeat jump.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"PLY16","name":"Box Jump + Stick Landing","video_id":"DDadUDHgiyU","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/DDadUDHgiyU","before":{"description":"Use a stable box at the height your coach assigns. Jump onto it, bend your knees as you land and hold your balance. Step down between jumps.","purpose":"Practise jumping onto a box and stabilizing the landing.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Land softly and stand steady. Avoid: Jumping back down between reps. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Use a stable box of the height Coach Du assigns. Jump onto it, land with hips, knees and ankles softly bent and hold balance; step down carefully before resetting. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise jumping onto a box and stabilizing the landing.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Land quietly. Knees follow toes. Stand balanced. Avoid: Chasing box height, landing near the edge or jumping down for extra contacts.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"POST01","name":"Hip-Lock Hold","video_id":"oWW7nZgqUNQ","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/oWW7nZgqUNQ","before":{"description":"Stand on one leg and use light support if needed. Raise the other knee as your coach shows you. Hold for the assigned time and keep breathing.","purpose":"Practise upright single-leg posture and pelvic control.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stay tall with hips facing forward. Avoid: Twisting to lift the knee higher. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Stand balanced on one leg, using light hand support if needed. Raise the other knee to the position shown and hold for the assigned time without twisting. Follow the assigned effort or time; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise upright single-leg posture and pelvic control.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stand tall. Hips level. Foot grounded. Avoid: Leaning sideways, gripping the floor excessively or lifting the knee by rounding the back.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"RUN01","name":"Progressive 40m Build-Up","video_id":"bj8mm2fTEfU","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/bj8mm2fTEfU","before":{"description":"Use a clear 40 m lane with room to slow down. Start relaxed, build to the assigned effort, then ease down past the finish.","purpose":"Prepare for faster running by gradually increasing speed.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Build speed a little at a time. Avoid: Going out at full speed. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Use a clear 40 m lane plus room to slow down. Begin relaxed and build smoothly to the assigned effort, then ease down beyond the finish. Follow the assigned effort or time; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Prepare for faster running by gradually increasing speed.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Build smoothly. Relax shoulders. Run through. Avoid: Sprinting hard from the first step, exceeding the assigned effort or stopping suddenly.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"SPR01","name":"A-March","video_id":"4lQsMyKRRn8","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/4lQsMyKRRn8","before":{"description":"March forward tall. Lift one knee with the opposite arm, put your foot down under you and switch sides.","purpose":"Practise upright marching rhythm and foot placement for running.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Step down under your hip. Avoid: Reaching your foot far out in front. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Stand tall on a clear lane. March forward with coordinated opposite arm and leg action, placing each foot under the body rather than reaching ahead. Follow the assigned effort or time; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise upright marching rhythm and foot placement for running.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Tall hips. Toes up. Step under you. Avoid: Leaning back, stamping the foot or lifting the knee by rounding the trunk.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"SPR02","name":"A-Skip","video_id":"V2OsnUiq4Ac","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/V2OsnUiq4Ac","before":{"description":"Skip forward with a steady beat. Lift one knee with the opposite arm, then make contact under you as you switch.","purpose":"Practise coordinated skipping rhythm for running.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stay tall and keep the beat. Avoid: Reaching forward to make each skip longer. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Use a clear lane and begin with a controlled skip. Lift one knee with the opposite arm and switch in a steady rhythm, contacting beneath the body. Follow the assigned effort or time; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise coordinated skipping rhythm for running.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Tall posture. Light skip. Match arms and legs. Avoid: Reaching forward with the foot, chasing knee height or rushing beyond coordination.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"SPR03","name":"Ankling","video_id":"U7e-InL5o04","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/U7e-InL5o04","before":{"description":"Stay tall on a clear lane. Take small, quick steps from the ankles as your coach shows you, placing your feet close under you.","purpose":"Practise low running contacts and ankle rhythm.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Quick steps under your hips. Avoid: Reaching for long steps. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Stand tall on a clear lane. Use the small ankle-led stepping action shown, moving forward gently with feet contacting close under the body. Follow the assigned effort or time; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise low running contacts and ankle rhythm.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Small steps. Light contacts. Tall hips. Avoid: Overstriding, excessive bouncing or forcing the ankles into a rigid position.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"SPR04","name":"Straight-Leg Run","video_id":"CmsZXZ61Iwg","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/CmsZXZ61Iwg","before":{"description":"Run along a clear lane at the assigned speed. Keep your legs long with a soft bend at the knees. Place each foot down close under your hip.","purpose":"Practise controlled leg cycling and contacts beneath the body.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Step down under your hips. Avoid: Locking the knees or kicking far out in front. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Use a clear lane and the speed demonstrated. Run with long legs and small, natural knee movement, striking down close beneath the hips rather than reaching ahead. Follow the assigned effort or time; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise controlled leg cycling and contacts beneath the body.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Long legs. Tall hips. Contact under you. Avoid: Locking the knees, leaning back or kicking the feet far in front.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"SPR05","name":"Dribble Run","video_id":"HKykH7ctpbo","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/HKykH7ctpbo","before":{"description":"Use the step height your coach shows you. Make small cycling steps under you as you move forward at the assigned speed.","purpose":"Practise compact running rhythm with feet working beneath the hips.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Small circles under your hips. Avoid: Reaching out in front instead of stepping down under you. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Use a clear lane and the dribble height shown. Make small cycling actions under the body while moving forward at the assigned speed. Follow the assigned effort or time; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise compact running rhythm with feet working beneath the hips.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Cycle small. Stay tall. Feet under hips. Avoid: Reaching ahead, lifting the knees beyond the assigned drill or rushing out of rhythm.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"SPR06","name":"Fast Feet → Run","video_id":"","video_url":"","before":{"description":"On a clear lane, start with the quick steps your coach assigns, then build into the run. Leave room to slow down.","purpose":"Practise moving from a quick-foot rhythm into a controlled run.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Quick feet, then build speed. Avoid: Trying to make the first running step too long. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"On a clear lane, perform the quick-foot action shown and transition into the assigned run. Keep arm and leg actions coordinated and allow room to slow down. Follow the assigned effort or time; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Practise moving from a quick-foot rhythm into a controlled run.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Quick rhythm. Smooth transition. Run through. Avoid: Stomping in place, forcing a sudden reach forward or adding unassigned sprint effort.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"STR01","name":"Split Squat","video_id":"fq72qz8JHtU","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/fq72qz8JHtU","before":{"description":"Stand with one foot ahead of the other. Bend both knees to the assigned depth, then push through your front foot to stand. Use support or weight as assigned.","purpose":"Develop single-leg strength and control in a split stance.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Keep your front foot flat. Avoid: Letting the front knee fall inward. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Stand in a stable split stance. Bend both knees to lower within the assigned range, then push through the front foot to return; use support or load only as prescribed. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Develop single-leg strength and control in a split stance.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Front foot grounded. Knee follows toes. Control down. Avoid: Knees collapsing inward, losing balance or forcing the rear knee onto the floor.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"STR02","name":"Step-Up","video_id":"Tdn9-s7-YPc","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/Tdn9-s7-YPc","before":{"description":"Use a firm step at the assigned height. Put your whole lead foot on it and push through that foot to stand up. Step down slowly.","purpose":"Develop single-leg strength and balance while stepping onto a box.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push through the foot on the step. Avoid: Springing off the foot on the ground. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Use a stable step of the assigned height and place the whole lead foot on it. Push through that leg to stand tall, then lower back down under control. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Develop single-leg strength and balance while stepping onto a box.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Whole foot on. Lead leg works. Slow down. Avoid: Jumping off the trailing leg, knee collapse or using a step too high to control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"STR03","name":"Single-Leg RDL","video_id":"o1SF5gKsVH0","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/o1SF5gKsVH0","before":{"description":"Stand on one leg with the knee slightly bent. Send your hips back as the other leg reaches behind. Stand back up and use support if assigned.","purpose":"Develop hip-hinge strength and single-leg balance.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Keep both hips facing the floor. Avoid: Turning the lifted hip out. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Stand on one leg with a soft knee and use support if assigned. Send the hips backward as the other leg reaches behind, then return tall while keeping the pelvis level. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Develop hip-hinge strength and single-leg balance.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Hips back. Long back. Hips face down. Avoid: Opening the pelvis, rounding the back or reaching lower than balance allows.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"STR04","name":"Reverse Lunge","video_id":"PPu6dREwL64","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/PPu6dREwL64","before":{"description":"Stand tall with room behind you. Step back and bend both knees to the assigned depth. Push through the front foot to stand.","purpose":"Develop controlled leg strength through a backward stepping action.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Push through the front foot. Avoid: Letting the front knee fall inward. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Stand tall with space behind you. Step back, bend both knees within a comfortable assigned range and push through the front foot to return. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Develop controlled leg strength through a backward stepping action.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Step back softly. Front foot grounded. Control the return. Avoid: Stepping onto a narrow line, knees collapsing inward or slamming the rear knee down.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"STR05","name":"Bridge Walkout","video_id":"EdyfB2_DkC8","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/EdyfB2_DkC8","before":{"description":"Lie on your back with your feet flat and lift your hips. Take small steps out and back on your heels as shown.","purpose":"Develop hamstring control while maintaining a bridge position.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Keep your hips steady. Avoid: Walking so far that your hips drop. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Lie on a mat, plant both feet and lift into a controlled bridge. Take small heel steps outward and back as demonstrated, shortening the distance if the hips cannot stay steady. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Develop hamstring control while maintaining a bridge position.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Small heel steps. Hips steady. Ribs settled. Avoid: Arching the back, letting hips drop or walking out beyond control.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"STR06","name":"Single-Leg Eccentric Box Squat — Explosive Up","video_id":"C6DJkHnaJH0","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/C6DJkHnaJH0","before":{"description":"Use a firm box at the assigned height. Lower slowly on the working leg to touch the box as shown. Drive up using the support or reset your coach assigns.","purpose":"Develop controlled single-leg lowering and a purposeful upward drive.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Slow down, then drive up. Avoid: Dropping onto the box or adding a jump. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Use a stable box at the assigned height. Lower on the working leg under control to the demonstrated box contact, then drive upward intentionally using the support or reset shown; do not add an unassigned jump. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Develop controlled single-leg lowering and a purposeful upward drive.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Lower slowly. Knee follows toes. Drive up with intent. Avoid: Dropping onto the box, rocking to escape the bottom position or adding load before control is reliable.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"STR07","name":"Supported Deep Knee Bend (Assisted Knee-Over-Toe Squat)","video_id":"OOH7c2sKip8","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/OOH7c2sKip8","before":{"description":"Hold a firm support and use the stance your coach shows you. Bend your knees as far as assigned and comfortable, then stand up slowly.","purpose":"Explore supported knee and ankle range with controlled leg strength.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stay in control as you lower. Avoid: Pulling yourself deeper than you can control. Stop if it hurts or you lose control.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Hold a stable support and match the stance shown. Lower into a comfortable supported knee bend, allowing the knee to travel as demonstrated, then return under control. Use only the assigned load and volume; stop if pain or loss of control develops.","purpose":"Explore supported knee and ankle range with controlled leg strength.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Use support. Follow the toes. Move comfortably. Avoid: Forcing depth, bouncing into the bottom or copying extra load or range not assigned.","admin_notes":"Import batch exercise-video-expansion-20. Exact mapping supplied and release authorized by Coach Du. Playback and movement verification pending; do not treat this entry as independently verified. Coaching sequence, setup, equipment and dosage require review; no default prescription supplied.\nCoaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"WU01","name":"Ankle Rock","video_id":"6Dlac5mxD6k","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/6Dlac5mxD6k","before":{"description":"Use the stance your coach assigns. Move the front knee forward over the foot while keeping the heel down, then ease back.","purpose":"Prepare the ankle for controlled forward knee travel.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Move the knee, keep the heel down. Avoid: Forcing the knee forward.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Use a split or kneeling stance and support as shown. Guide the front knee forward over the foot while the heel remains grounded, then return slowly. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Prepare the ankle for controlled forward knee travel.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Heel down. Knee follows toes. Easy range. Avoid: Lifting the heel, collapsing the arch or forcing a painful range.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"WU02","name":"Straight-Leg Hamstring Kick","video_id":"UEzzeExMLLw","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/UEzzeExMLLw","before":{"description":"Walk forward and lift one leg at a time with the knee nearly straight. Lift only as high as feels comfortable and lower slowly.","purpose":"Prepare the back of the thigh through controlled leg swings while walking.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stay tall as the leg lifts. Avoid: Throwing the leg up or leaning back.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Stand tall with space ahead. Walk forward and lift one long leg within a comfortable range, then lower with control and alternate. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Prepare the back of the thigh through controlled leg swings while walking.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stay tall. Reach comfortably. Control down. Avoid: Leaning back, snapping the knee straight or forcing the foot higher.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"WU03","name":"Walking Lunge + Rotation","video_id":"e6BRge-9RdY","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/e6BRge-9RdY","before":{"description":"Step into a walking lunge. Keep your front foot flat and turn your chest toward the front leg as shown. Face forward again before the next step.","purpose":"Prepare the hips and trunk with a controlled lunge and turn.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Keep the front foot flat as you turn. Avoid: Letting your front knee fall inward as you turn.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Step into a comfortable walking lunge. Keep the front foot grounded and rotate the chest toward the front leg as shown, then return and step through. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Prepare the hips and trunk with a controlled lunge and turn.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stable foot. Turn through chest. Stay controlled. Avoid: Forcing a long stride, twisting the front knee or rushing the rotation.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"WU04","name":"Adductor Rock-Back","video_id":"VQOIhPcPNZA","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/VQOIhPcPNZA","before":{"description":"Start on hands and knees. Straighten one leg out to the side as shown. Move your hips gently back, then come forward again.","purpose":"Explore inner-thigh mobility with a controlled hip rock.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Rock back slowly. Avoid: Forcing the stretch.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Start on hands and knees on a mat and extend one leg to the side as demonstrated. Rock the hips backward in a gentle range and return slowly. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Explore inner-thigh mobility with a controlled hip rock.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Hips back. Long back. Gentle range. Avoid: Forcing the stretch, rounding deeply or continuing through groin or knee pain.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"WU05","name":"High-Knee Hip Rotation Out","video_id":"ZchkCbWjOXw","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/ZchkCbWjOXw","before":{"description":"Stand tall and hold a firm support if needed. Lift one knee, circle it outward and bring the foot down slowly. Switch legs as assigned.","purpose":"Prepare controlled outward rotation of the hip.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stand tall as the knee circles. Avoid: Twisting your whole body with the knee.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Stand tall with support if needed. Lift one knee and open the hip outward through a comfortable arc, then return and alternate as assigned. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Prepare controlled outward rotation of the hip.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Tall body. Quiet pelvis. Move from hip. Avoid: Twisting the whole trunk, forcing the knee outward or losing balance to gain range.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"WU06","name":"Leg Swing Front / Back","video_id":"nL-SiujsIMk","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/nL-SiujsIMk","before":{"description":"Stand beside a firm support and hold it lightly. Swing one leg forward and back in a comfortable range.","purpose":"Prepare front-to-back hip movement with controlled leg swings.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Keep your upper body still. Avoid: Swinging so high that your back arches.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Stand beside a stable support. Swing one leg gently forward and backward while the pelvis and trunk stay steady; build only the comfortable range shown. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Prepare front-to-back hip movement with controlled leg swings.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Stand tall. Easy swing. Quiet trunk. Avoid: Forcing height, arching the back or swinging beyond balance.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}},{"code":"WU07","name":"Leg Swing Side / Side","video_id":"7euYeH7erNw","video_url":"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/7euYeH7erNw","before":{"description":"Face a firm support and hold it lightly. Swing one leg across your body and back out to the side in a comfortable range.","purpose":"Prepare side-to-side hip movement with controlled leg swings.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Keep your hips facing forward. Avoid: Turning your whole body with the leg.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."},"after":{"description":"Face a stable support and hold it lightly. Swing one leg across and away from the body within a comfortable range, keeping the pelvis mostly forward. Keep the movement comfortable; do not force a stretch.","purpose":"Prepare side-to-side hip movement with controlled leg swings.","coaching_cues":"Cue: Tall body. Easy rhythm. Control the return. Avoid: Twisting the whole trunk, forcing range or swinging into another person.","admin_notes":"Coaching audit 2026-11-15: named-exercise-text-reviewed; demo-not-independently-verified. Library guidance does not change assigned prescriptions."}}]$changes$::jsonb;
  row_data jsonb;
  current_content jsonb;
  protected_before jsonb;
  protected_after jsonb;
  programme_before jsonb;
  programme_after jsonb;
BEGIN
  LOCK TABLE public.exercises IN SHARE ROW EXCLUSIVE MODE;
  LOCK TABLE public.programmes,public.programme_weeks,public.training_days,public.session_blocks,public.saved_blocks,public.saved_block_items,public.athlete_overrides,public.cohort_overrides,public.athletes,public.cohorts,public.professional_members,public.programme_versions,public.feedback,public.workout_item_completions IN SHARE MODE;
  SELECT jsonb_object_agg(e.code,to_jsonb(e)-ARRAY['description','purpose','coaching_cues','admin_notes','updated_at']) INTO protected_before FROM public.exercises e;
  programme_before := jsonb_build_object('programmes',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.programmes t),'programme_weeks',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.programme_weeks t),'training_days',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.training_days t),'session_blocks',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.session_blocks t),'saved_blocks',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.saved_blocks t),'saved_block_items',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.saved_block_items t),'athlete_overrides',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.athlete_overrides t),'cohort_overrides',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.cohort_overrides t),'athletes',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.athletes t),'cohorts',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.cohorts t),'professional_members',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.professional_members t),'programme_versions',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.programme_versions t),'feedback',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.feedback t),'workout_item_completions',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.workout_item_completions t));
  IF jsonb_array_length(changes) <> 85 THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Expected 85 audited entries'; END IF;
  FOR row_data IN SELECT value FROM jsonb_array_elements(changes) LOOP
    SELECT jsonb_build_object('description',e.description,'purpose',e.purpose,'coaching_cues',e.coaching_cues,'admin_notes',e.admin_notes) INTO current_content FROM public.exercises e
      WHERE code=row_data->>'code' AND name=row_data->>'name'
        AND video_id IS NOT DISTINCT FROM row_data->>'video_id'
        AND video_url IS NOT DISTINCT FROM row_data->>'video_url';
    IF NOT FOUND THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Exercise identity/video changed: %',row_data->>'code'; END IF;
    IF current_content = row_data->'after' THEN CONTINUE; END IF;
    IF current_content IS DISTINCT FROM row_data->'before' THEN
      RAISE EXCEPTION 'Concurrent coaching edit: %; re-audit before updating',row_data->>'code';
    END IF;
    UPDATE public.exercises SET description=row_data->'after'->>'description',
      coaching_cues=row_data->'after'->>'coaching_cues',updated_at=now()
      WHERE code=row_data->>'code';
  END LOOP;
  IF EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM jsonb_array_elements(changes) r JOIN public.exercises e ON e.code=r->>'code'
    WHERE jsonb_build_object('description',e.description,'purpose',e.purpose,'coaching_cues',e.coaching_cues,'admin_notes',e.admin_notes) IS DISTINCT FROM r->'after') THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Coaching content persistence mismatch'; END IF;
  SELECT jsonb_object_agg(e.code,to_jsonb(e)-ARRAY['description','purpose','coaching_cues','admin_notes','updated_at']) INTO protected_after FROM public.exercises e;
  IF protected_before IS DISTINCT FROM protected_after THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Protected exercise fields changed'; END IF;
  programme_after := jsonb_build_object('programmes',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.programmes t),'programme_weeks',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.programme_weeks t),'training_days',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.training_days t),'session_blocks',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.session_blocks t),'saved_blocks',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.saved_blocks t),'saved_block_items',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.saved_block_items t),'athlete_overrides',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.athlete_overrides t),'cohort_overrides',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.cohort_overrides t),'athletes',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.athletes t),'cohorts',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.cohorts t),'professional_members',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.professional_members t),'programme_versions',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.programme_versions t),'feedback',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.feedback t),'workout_item_completions',(select md5(coalesce(string_agg(to_jsonb(t)::text,'' order by id),'')) from public.workout_item_completions t));
  IF programme_before IS DISTINCT FROM programme_after THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Approved programme content changed'; END IF;
END
$coaching$;
